Virtual-F
=========

Virtual-F is a Hypervisor and a Emulator writted in Assembly, no high-level languages, no abstractions. 

Quick Start 
------------
Find your first start:
  * LLM or AI Assistant: See Documentation/AI-LLM/coding-assistant.
  * Maintainer and reviewing patches: See Documentation/Review/Reviewing.rst.
  * See more of maintainers: See MAINTAINERS or Subsystem/.
  * License: See LICENSE and SPDX-Identifier.
  * Assembly Developer: See the code.
  * Build: See .devcontainer/ or .github/workflows/.
  * Editor Syntax: See .editorconfig.
  * Git: See .gitattributes or .gitignore.
  * Docker: See .devcontainer/ and .dockerignore.

Objective 
----------
Virtual-F objectives:
   * Superate QEMU.
   * Domain all Archs (RISC-V, MIPS, ARM etc).

